ght)=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule and then the product rule for logarithms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln\\left(\\frac{p}{e\\cdot 3}\\right) &= \\ln\\left(p\\right)-\\ln\\left(e\\cdot 3\\right) \\\\ &= -\\ln\\left(e\\right)-\\ln\\left(3\\right)+\\ln\\left(p\\right) \\\\ &= -1-\\ln\\left(3\\right)+\\ln\\left(p\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\ln\\left(e\\right)=1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186608308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5083e127-e679-5fdb-a46b-056ff2dc2b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log\\left(\\frac{x}{9\\cdot z}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608291} {:answer/id #uuid "6d52e434-ca9c-59db-ae6d-87003cd6dfd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log\\left(\\frac{9}{z\\cdot x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608295} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd10e3c-2577-513c-91e0-b6fe75983139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608297} {:answer/id #uuid "b0156c05-cb60-5d69-814f-afae9d22b94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log\\left(\\frac{z}{9\\cdot x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608307} {:answer/id #uuid "fdca327f-47e4-562a-a7ea-3e52767dd3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log\\left(\\frac{z\\cdot x}{9}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dd10e3c-2577-513c-91e0-b6fe75983139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608297} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d0ddddd-6a9c-5691-90dc-4ea259771bf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186608301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3d53eb1-c5f0-51f3-be9a-3c9eb88f1d03" :question/problem "Express $\\log\\left(9\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right)$ as a single logarithm. Assume $z>0$ and $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, combine the logarithms with the same sign. Then use the quotient rule to subtract the denominator logarithm:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log\\left(9\\right)+\\log\\left(z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) &= \\log\\left(9\\cdot z\\right)-\\log\\left(x\\right) \\\\ &= \\log\\left(\\frac{9\\cdot z}{x}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting an Expression Using the Product and Quotient Rules of Logarithms"}]
